Id: shl003w
Severity: WARN
Category: filesystem
Check: check_ttys
Fix: Mark the console insecure in /etc/ttys.
References: ttys(5); init(8)
Controls: CIS 4.1; NIST AC-3, IA-2; ISO 8.5, 8.9; CE Secure configuration

The console line in /etc/ttys carries no insecure flag: it is marked
secure, or carries no flag at all. Such a console drops to single-user
mode without asking for the root password, so anyone at the machine
who can reach the boot prompt is root. FreeBSD ships the console
secure, as Linux ships single-user mode without a password until the
boot loader is locked; both are reported the same way. Mark the
console insecure and init asks for the root password first:
  console none  unknown off insecure
